---
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CatalogCard from '../../../components/CatalogCard.astro';
import CategoryHubDetail from '../../../components/product/CategoryHubDetail.astro';
import StatusNotice from '../../../components/StatusNotice.astro';
import { getGroup, productHref, productsInGroup } from '../../../data/products.js';
import { productImageAlt } from '../../../utils/product-page.js';
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const group = getGroup('fire-retardant-resins');
const items = productsInGroup('fire-retardant-resins');
---
<Base
  title="Fire Retardant Resins — Supplier & Importer in Nepal"
  description="Fire retardant resin products supplied and imported by Samrat FRP Traders for buyers across Nepal, with supplier-issued technical documentation."
>
  <section class="page-hero hero-shell">
    <div class="hero-grid-lines" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="container page-hero-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product category</p>
      <h1>{group.name}</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">Fire retardant resin products supplied and imported for the Nepal market.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { label: 'Home', href: '/en/' },
          { label: 'Products', href: '/en/products/' },
          { label: group.name },
        ]}
      />

      <div class="category-intro" data-reveal>
        <p>
          Fire retardant grades are specified where a project, a client or a regulation calls for defined
          fire behaviour. That requirement usually arrives as a named standard or classification, and the
          only meaningful way to answer it is with the supplier's own published test data for the exact
          grade — not with a general product description.
        </p>
        <p>
          Samrat FRP Traders supplies and imports these products as a trader. We do not conduct fire testing
          and we do not issue fire ratings or classifications. Where your specification names a standard,
          send it with your enquiry so the requirement can be checked against the supplier's current
          documentation before anything is committed.
        </p>
        <p>
          The two grades stocked here differ in fire-retardant chemistry rather than in handling.
          One uses a halogenated formulation; the other is isophthalic-based with a halogen-free,
          ATH-filled formulation. Their published viscosity, gel time and styrene content are
          identical, so choosing between them is a formulation decision rather than a processing
          one. One naming point causes regular confusion and is worth stating plainly: the "ISO"
          in ISO Fire Retardant Resin refers to isophthalic chemistry — it is not a reference to
          ISO certification.
        </p>
      </div>

      <StatusNotice
        title="Fire performance claims"
        message="Any fire rating, class or test result for these products is issued by the manufacturer for a specific grade and must be read from the current supplier technical data sheet. Samrat FRP Traders performs no fire testing and makes no independent fire performance claim."
      />

      <div class="category-grid" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        {items.map((product) => (
          <CatalogCard
            name={product.name}
            eyebrow={group.name}
            href={productHref(product, '/en')}
            showMedia
            image={product.images?.[0]}
            imageAlt={productImageAlt(product, false)}
            ctaLabel="View product"
          />
        ))}
      </div>

      <CategoryHubDetail groupSlug="fire-retardant-resins" lang="en" />

      <div class="section-actions" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        <a class="button" href="/en/products/">View full catalogue</a>
        <a class="button" href="/en/documents/">Document library</a>
        <a class="button" href="/en/contact/">Send an enquiry</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    min-height: clamp(14rem, 26vh, 19rem);
  }

  .page-hero-content {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .section:first-of-type {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .category-intro {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-block: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  .category-intro p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .category-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(16rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
</style>
